hadiths[9]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15555","al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us: al-Awzai narrated to us, he said: I heard Yahya ibn Abi Kathir saying: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Asad ibn Zurarah narrated to me, from Qays ibn Sad, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited us in our house and said: Peace upon you and the mercy of Allah. He said: So Sad responded with a faint response. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned, and Sad followed him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I used to hear your salam and respond to you with a faint response, that you multiply salam upon us. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned back with him. So Sad ordered ghusl for him, and it was placed, and he washed. Then he handed him, or he said: they handed him, a wrapper dyed with saffron and wars, and he wrapped himself with it. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his hands, saying: O Allah, place Your prayers and Your mercy upon the family of Sad ibn Ubadah. He said: Then he ate of the food. When he intended to leave, Sad brought near to him a donkey saddled with velvet, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rode. Sad said: O Qays, accompany the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Qays said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ride. But I refused. Then he said: Either you ride, or you leave. He said: So I left."
"15556","Waki narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Abu Ammar, from Qays ibn Sad, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to fast Ashura before the fasting of Ramadan was sent down. When the fasting of Ramadan was sent down, he neither ordered us nor forbade us, and we do it."
"15557","Abdullah ibn Yazid Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Haywah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Mulayl informed me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Umayyah, that Habib ibn Maslamah came to Qays ibn Sad ibn Ubadah in the first fitnah while he was upon a horse. So he moved back from the saddle and said: Ride. But he refused. Qays ibn Sad said to him: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The owner of the mount is most entitled to its front. Habib said to him: I am not ignorant of what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, but I fear for you."
"15558","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us: Israil narrated to us, from Jabir, from Amir, from Qays ibn Sad ibn Ubadah, he said: There is nothing that was at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but I have seen it, except one thing: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to have qals performed for him on the day of al-Fitr. Jabir said: It is play."
"15559","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us: My father narrated to us, he said: I heard Mansur ibn Zadham narrating, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from Qays ibn Sad ibn Ubadah, that his father gave him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to serve him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon me while I had prayed two rakahs. He struck me with his foot and said: Shall I not guide you to a gate of the gates of Paradise? I said: Yes. He said: There is no might nor power except by Allah."
"15560","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub informed me, from Ubaydillah ibn Zahr, from Bakr ibn Sawadah, from Qays ibn Sad ibn Ubadah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My Lord the Blessed and Exalted forbade me wine and the kubah and the qinnin, and beware of ghubayra, for it is a third of the wine of the world."
"15561","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Hubayrah narrated to me, he said: I heard a shaykh of Himyar narrating to Abu Tamim al-Jayshani that he heard Qays ibn Sad ibn Ubadah al-Ansari, while he was over Egypt, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take a resting place of Fire, or a house in Jahannam."
"15562","I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever drinks wine will come thirsty on the Day of Resurrection. Verily every intoxicant is wine, and beware of ghubayra."
"15563","This shaykh said: Then I heard Abdullah ibn Amr after that saying like it, and they differed only in house or resting place."
